desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Detect PseudoRandomBytes"
	title_zh: "Detect PseudoRandomBytes"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-detect-pseudoRandomBytes"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `detect-pseudoRandomBytes` (javascript/lang/security/detect-pseudoRandomBytes.yaml).
Original message: Detected usage of crypto.pseudoRandomBytes, which does not produce secure random numbers.
CWE: CWE-338: Use of Cryptographically Weak Pseudo-Random Number Generator (PRNG)
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A02_2021-Cryptographic_Failures
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.js": <<<POS
crypto.pseudoRandomBytes
POS
	"safefile://pos.js": <<<NEG
crypto.randomBytes
NEG
)

${*.js}.pattern_regex(/(?:crypto\.pseudoRandomBytes)/) as $p0
${*.ts}.pattern_regex(/(?:crypto\.pseudoRandomBytes)/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Detect PseudoRandomBytes",
	title_zh: "Detect PseudoRandomBytes",
	message: "Detect PseudoRandomBytes detected.",
}
